text:
Marie: Quick sync — we need a product decision for structured-output behavior for our prioritized customers (FinReg). Customer asks for strict JSON Schema enforcement but they also care about latency. Options on the table: client-side schema validation + server retry, server-side strict with fallback to text mode, or soft validation with telemetry. Thoughts?
Rohit: Staged approach seems safest. Default to `warn` for now, offer `validation_level=strict` opt-in. Rollout: warn -> soft-enforce (auto-retry) -> strict over 2-3 sprints. Allows prompt tuning.
Sara: Agree. Also we need a clear error taxonomy so apps can programmatically react. Minimal codes: `schema_mismatch`, `missing_required`, `type_mismatch`, `extraneous_fields`. Responses should include a machine-readable error block: `validation_error: {code, path, message}`. Example schema that customers might pass: 
```json
{
  "$id": "https://redwood.ai/schemas/invoice-1.json",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["invoice_id", "amount"],
  "properties": {
    "invoice_id": {"type": "string"},
    "amount": {"type": "number"},
    "items": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "sku": {"type": "string"},
          "qty": {"type": "integer"}
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
Alex: For API surface, propose `validation_level` with values `[off, warn, strict]` and a `retry_policy` object. Example request payload: 
```json
{
  "model": "redwood-chat-xl",
  "mode": "json",
  "schema": "<json-schema>",
  "validation_level": "warn",
  "retry_policy": {"on": "schema_mismatch", "max_attempts": 2, "backoff": "exponential"}
}
```
Rohit: Important: where do retries happen? Server-side one internal retry could happen for cheap fixes (e.g., minor cast fixes) before surfacing to client when `validation_level=warn`. For `strict` we might want the server to keep retrying up to limit, or surface an explicit `validation_error` after exhausting attempts. Need budget guardrails.
Eric: Telemetry: emit `validation_fail_rate`, `retry_rate`, `avg_validation_latency_ms`, and `validation_false_reject_rate` per model/route. We must cap server retries' added latency — requirement: p95 added latency < 150ms for warn mode. Also track cost delta.
Marie: Draft launch criteria proposal: default = `warn`. GA requires: false-rejects <= 1% on our evaluation suites for top 10 customer schemas, p95 added latency < 150ms, SDKs support flags + examples, console shows per-model default. `strict` gated behind enterprise flag and canary rollout. Docs + backward compatibility notes required.
ci-bot: CI checklist added: unit test for schema validation logic, e2e tests for retry behavior, integration tests for `validation_error` payload format, update changelog, console UI toggle, and SDK feature flag tests.
Sara: I'll draft the spec doc (error schema, example schemas, prompt tuning guide) and a short eval harness to compute false-rejects. Expect PR by Wed. :thumbsup:
Alex: SDK work: add `validation_level` + pass-through `schema` to server; also expose `validation_error` type in SDK error classes. I'll open an issue and pair with Sara.
Rohit: I'll write rollout plan: canary percentages, telemetry thresholds, and automatic rollback rules if validation_fail_rate spikes.
Marie: Action items recap: Sara => spec + eval harness PR by Wed; Alex => SDK issue + owner; Rohit => rollout plan + telemetry events; Eric => add metrics to observability backlog. Ping me on blockers.
Marie: Thanks everyone — we'll sync again after the spec draft.
